    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d28">

                <pb facs="0106" n="32" sameAs="frus:frus1918Russiav01/pg32"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/4093</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic"> Baron Rosen </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d28-f1"/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">to President Wilson </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Petrograd</hi></placeName>, <date
                            ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content-and-sibling-dates"
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-25"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >undated</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received April
                            25, 1917, 6.29 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Public meeting convened in Petrograd town hall by Society for Promoting Friendly
                    Relations between Russia and America.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d28-f2"/> After being
                    addressed by American Ambassador and Foreign Minister sends <pb facs="0107"
                        n="33" xml:id="pg33"/> to you and the American people whom you represent in
                    such noble way its fraternal greetings and expression of admiration for your
                    constant upholding of the great principles of freedom and right. We are deeply
                    convinced that our two countries which represent the greatest democracies of the
                    world will remain forever closely united and work in common for the progress of
                    humanity.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Baron Rosen</hi>
                    </signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Chairman</hi>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d28-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d28-f1-content">
                <p>Russian Ambassador at Washington, 1905–11.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d28-f2" n="2" xml:id="d28-f2-content">
                <p>For the account by the Ambassador in Russia of the Russian-American meeting of
                    Apr. 23 in the hall of the City Duma at Petrograd, mainly devoted to
                    denunciations of the idea of a separate peace, see his telegram No. 1217, Apr.
                    24, 1917, <ref target="frus1917Supp02v01">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Foreign Relations</hi>, 1917, Supplement 2, vol. <hi
                            rendition="#small-caps">i</hi></ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
